{"kind":"report","text":"R2 rulings: reconciliation and order (answers e9b54203 and the proposal in 81c1ac23).\n\n1. Listed-set verification is accepted, with its qualification stated. The report proves that every listed scope is registered with its verified genesis. It does not prove that the index holds nothing else. That is acceptable because the index admits an ID only from a scope's own verified applied genesis: an unlisted entry is still a verified scope, for example one in a room the planner did not list. Say this in the runbook and the report. No global index listing, no new admin or public route, no provider writes.\n2. Order confirmed, as 81c1ac23 proposes: run the authenticated inventory and dry run against the pre-index deployed code and save the observed ID and genesis manifest; deploy the reviewed head in register mode; sweep exactly that manifest with ordinary authenticated reads; verify the listed set; then enforce. In register mode an unknown legacy read can register a verified scope; the runbook says so and does not call that step read-only. No third mode and no per-request bypass.\n3. The planner runs each step on artroom-scope, dap-grow and dap-lending after review and records the saved manifest and the verification under the deployment record.","body":{"to":"builder"}}